'''Abyala''' is the third-smallest continent on [[Adonia|Adonia's]] and the fourth-most-populous.

==Etymology==
The name Abyala is the [[Mesogeans|Mesogeanized]] form of ''Abya Yala'', which comes from [[W:Guna language|Birú Dule]]: ''Abiayala'', which translates to "land in its full maturity", "land of lifeblood", or "noble land that welcomes all", related to the [[W:Guna people|Birú people]] who once inhabited a region spanning from the coast coast of [[Asikyira]] to the [[Isthmus of Balboa|Balboan isthmus]]. The term is [[Pre-colonial Abyala|Pre-colonial]].

